## Your bill at a glance
kpi Service charge | $14.50 | per month, fixed | neutral
kpi Delivery charge | $0.045 | per kWh | neutral
kpi Peak supply | $0.31 | per kWh, weekday afternoons and evenings | neutral

Your bill has three main parts: a fixed monthly service charge, a delivery charge for each kilowatt-hour (kWh) you use, and a supply charge that depends on when you use power. Sales tax of 5.2% applies to the total.

## What each charge means
- **Service charge:** $14.50 a month, whatever you use.
- **Delivery charge:** $0.045 for each kWh.
- **Supply charge:** the power itself. It costs $0.31 per kWh at peak, $0.12 off-peak and $0.08 super off-peak.

Peak power costs more than 2.5 times as much as off-peak power, so when you use it matters.

## Time-of-use hours
table = Period,Hours,Supply per kWh; Peak,16:00 to 21:00 on weekdays,$0.31; Off-peak,Everything else,$0.12; Super off-peak,00:00 to 06:00 every day,$0.08

## Ways to lower your bill
- Run the dishwasher and laundry after 21:00.
- Precool the house before 16:00. During peak hours, set the thermostat 2 degrees higher.
- Charge electric vehicles after midnight.

Your bill is due 21 days after the bill date. After that, a late payment fee of 1.5% is added to unpaid balances. Budget billing spreads your year into 12 equal payments, which we review every 6 months.

Income-qualified households can get a 20% discount through the CARE program. Enrolling takes about 10 minutes online.

Call 800-555-0166 or use the online account page for help.
